      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Under a strict liability framework, the developer’s defense is not an explanation of the model's 'why,' but a demonstration that the system’s error rate remains within defined, acceptable safety bounds.",
      "targets": [
        "AN-35"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Expectations of internal logic inspection for high-dimensional models seek a 'ghost in the machine' narrative that does not exist.",
      "targets": [
